<title>SINGAPORE: Zhuzhou says zinc problem with Glencore resolved.</title>
<headline>Zhuzhou says zinc problem with Glencore resolved.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's Zhuzhou smelter confirmed on Monday the company involved in questioning the quality of its London Metal Exchange-registered zinc Torch brand was Swiss trader Glencore and the problem had been resolved.</p>
<p>&quot;The problem was with Glencore and this has now been resolved,&quot; a Zhenzhou source told Reuters by telephone.</p>
<p>Earlier on Monday, the smelter issued a statement saying a claim made to to the LME that the Torch brand did not meet the exchange's quality standards had been withdrawn by the company involved.  </p>
<p>Officials at Glencore offices around the region could not be reached for comment.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom, +65 870-3174</p>
</text>
